    rdfs:label "Evidence for Spirits used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 978"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "It is commonly used for pictures. Spirit varnishes. When resins are dissolved in alcohol, commonly called spirit of wine, the varnish dries very speedily, but is subject to crack."@en ;
